you comes down the stair into the hedge.
The Hedge (dodecahedron, twenty caves of three tunnels, seed 7). Find the far gate. Type help for the words.
The Mouth of the Hedge
A stair goes up behind you. A plate is set in the rock beside it.
Tunnels lead left to 10, ahead to 2 and right to 16.
> read
Twenty caves, three tunnels each, and no dead ends. There is no north here: left and right are from the tunnel you came by. A hand on the wall goes round in five and comes back.
> study
Twenty caves, three tunnels each, laid out as the twelve-sided die, the old Wumpus map. A hand on the wall walks one face of the die: five caves, and back where you began. Hamilton's walk visits every cave once and comes home: from the stair go ahead, then left left left right right right left right left right, and again. It works from any tunnel, because every tunnel of the die is like every other. Where the gate is, a draft blows.
> north
There is no north in this hedge. Its ways are the tunnels, by number, and left, right and back from the tunnel you came by, and up and down where there is a stair.
> turn left
In a cave you do not face or turn. Left and right are from the tunnel you came by; back is that tunnel.
> back
Rock. No tunnel leads that way.
> look
The Mouth of the Hedge
A stair goes up behind you. A plate is set in the rock beside it.
Tunnels lead left to 10, ahead to 2 and right to 16.
> ahead
Cave 2
Tunnels lead left to 11, right to 4 and back to 17.
> left
Cave 11
Tunnels lead left to 15, right to 13 and back to 2.
> map
Caves you have stood in, and their tunnels:
   2: 17 4 11
  11: 15 2 13  (you are here)
  17: 16 2 10
Heard of: 4 10 13 15 16.
> score
2 turns. 28 turns of light and 2 torches to come. Your back to cave 2.
> again
You go back to the mouth of the hedge with fresh torches.
The Mouth of the Hedge
A stair goes up behind you. A plate is set in the rock beside it.
Tunnels lead left to 10, ahead to 2 and right to 16.
> cast (turn left)
The spell does not hold (chibi): (turn left): in a cave you do not face or turn; left and right are from the tunnel you came by
> cast
Type the spell. A blank line ends it.
  . (go ahead)
  . (until (gate?)
  .   (go left) (go left) (go left)
  .   (go right) (go right) (go right)
  .   (go left) (go right) (go left) (go right))
  . 
The spell holds (chibi). It runs one step a turn; stop ends it.
